{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.twoAlphaD_not_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.twoAlphaD_not_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseBarMixedD.lean#L53-L62","doc":"**α_D is NOT bar-odd** at any admissible substrate point (`q ∉ {0, ±1}`): its\nbar-even part `(q²−1)²/q²` is strictly positive, so it cannot vanish the way a\npure bar-odd phase would. This is the obstruction: no D analog of the C\neven-channel pin exists via the bar involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.twoAlphaD_bar_even_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.twoAlphaD_bar_even_sum","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseBarMixedD.lean#L41-L51","doc":"**α_D's bar-even part is nonzero (closed form).** Under `q ↦ q⁻¹`,\n`2α_D(1/q) + 2α_D(q) = (q²−1)²/q²`. A pure bar-odd phase would give `0`\n(cf. `α_C`, `QOU.Interactions.eigenphase_bar_involution`); this is the\nD-frame contrast. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.twoAlphaD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.twoAlphaD","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseBarMixedD.lean#L37-L39","doc":"Twice the D rung phase, `2α_D(q) = (z_D(q) − 1)·h(q)` — the counit-minus-trace\ngap in the D frame. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.heckeH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.heckeH","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseBarMixedD.lean#L34-L35","doc":"Hecke–Skein differential `h(q) = q − q⁻¹` (bar-odd). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.EigenphaseBarMixedD.zD","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/EigenphaseBarMixedD.lean#L30-L32","doc":"Convention-D Markov parameter (sqrt-free): `z_D(q) = q³/(q²+1)`. Matches the\ncanonical `QOU.BraidKnot.JonesNuclearQuotient.markovZ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}